Mark S. is the main protagonist of the Apple TV+ series "Severance," played by Adam Scott. Here''s a breakdown of who he is:

*   **Innie:** Mark is an employee at Lumon Industries who has undergone the "severance" procedure. This procedure surgically divides an employee''s memories between their work life (the "innie") and personal life (the "outie"). As an "innie" at Lumon, Mark works in the Macrodata Refinement (MDR) department. He''s seen as a conscientious and somewhat reserved employee who follows protocol. He is promoted to department head after the departure of Petey Kilmer.
*   **Outie:** Outside of Lumon, Mark is a grieving widower. His wife, Gemma, died in a car accident a couple of years prior to the start of the series. He initially chose severance as a way to escape his grief during the workday. He teaches a grief support group.
*   **Key Conflicts and Mysteries:** Mark is central to the show''s mysteries. Throughout the first season, both his "innie" and "outie" selves begin to question the nature of Lumon and the severance procedure. His "innie" is particularly driven by the reappearance of his best friend Petey, who was his fellow employee before his unexpected death. His "outie" experiences unsettling events, suggesting that his "innie''s" actions are affecting his life outside of work, and meets a woman who bears an uncanny resemblance to his deceased wife.
